  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xe9;ponse d&#x2019;urgence aux r&#xe9;fugi&#xe9;s affect&#xe9;s par les inondations dans les camps des r&#xe9;fugi&#xe9;s de N&#x2019;Djamena, Sila, Chari-Baguirmi et le Lac</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main aim of this $900,000 UNHCR project is to provide multi-sectoral emergency assistance to refugees affected by the floods in Chad. To that end, UNHCR will provide shelter (in-kind and through cash), distribute NFI kits, rehabilitate water points, distribute water treatment products and hygiene kits, install latrines, raise awareness around hygiene and health, train health personnel in refugee camps and provide essential medicines, and provide temporary learning spaces. In total, UNHCR will target 21,294 people, including 7,881 women and 4,069 girls. Among those targeted UNHCR expects to be 305 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
